1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,073
Part five is OpenUI Lang. The model writes a small program instead of JSON, and the page re-parses it on every chunk.

2
00:00:10,073 --> 00:00:21,209
This is a program. root refers to title, kpis, split and actions before they are defined, which is called hoisting, and it is what makes streaming work.

3
00:00:21,209 --> 00:00:32,237
Arguments are positional, so each component has a fixed signature. HtmlArtifact maps to our sandboxed HtmlView, and SalesOverview is the pre-built static component.

4
00:00:32,237 --> 00:00:44,270
parse() with partial=True skips the line that is still being written. resolve() turns names that are not defined yet into placeholders.

5
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:53,310
The same resolver in JavaScript, which the browser runs after every streamed chunk.

6
00:00:53,310 --> 00:01:04,348
Actions: the app answers drill_region by appending lines. A later root = ... replaces the earlier one.

7
00:01:04,348 --> 00:01:19,463
In the terminal: the program as streamed, its size compared with the JSON tree, and the terminal render after the click.

8
00:01:19,463 --> 00:01:28,629
Static: a single line, root = SalesOverview(...).

9
00:01:28,629 --> 00:01:42,788
Declarative: placeholders fill in as forward references get defined. The program here is about 60% of the size of the same UI as JSON.

10
00:01:42,788 --> 00:01:53,047
Open-ended: root = HtmlArtifact(...). The document mounts once its line is complete.

11
00:01:53,047 --> 00:02:01,215
Mixed: catalog components plus one HtmlArtifact.

12
00:02:01,215 --> 00:02:10,338
The tests cover forward references, partial programs, positional props, the rules for each mode, and the appended action.

